  "model": {
    "change": "Reuse the existing bounded inert-typography validator in every shared declaration target. Explicit baselines, anchors, font/paint spans and path placement retain their existing implementation. Inert numeric tokens use the common no-whitespace number styles and CSS-only boundary trimming.",
    "boundary": "The admitted CSS pre uses legacy XML-preserve normalization, replacing tabs/newlines with spaces. Automatic SVG2 line boxes and leading remain outside the contract. Pinned native behavior agrees with the single-line controls; this is not SVG2 automatic-line-layout acceptance.",
    "specification": "https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG2/text.html#LineHeightProperty",
    "specificationReading": "SVG2 uses line-height for leading between automatic lines, not text on a path. Its CSS-pre forced-line layout is distinct from legacy XML normalization. The implementation retains explicit-position layout rather than adding an unused line-height field.",
    "unknownDeclarations": "Unknown CSS names still reject through the common parser, including stroke-fill. No source-name exception or unimplemented-property registry is added; ny1 remains unsupported and its general declaration-semantics review remains open."
  },
